# One line ending everywhere: LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout gets CRLF while any tool that rewrites a
# file — a formatter, a codegen step, tidy_imports itself — writes LF, and
# every diff fills up with whole-file changes that are really just \r.
#
# It does not change what tidy_imports does to *your* files: the CLI detects
# each file's existing ending and puts it back.
* text=auto eol=lf
